{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "05-archon-providers-map",
  "title": "Archon providers and the kernel",
  "description": "How Archon calls agents today and where Ford's agent kernel would plug in.\n\n- **Archon engine**: the DAG executor reads Capabilities (preflight), then calls sendQuery on **IAgentProvider**. sendQuery yields a Chunk stream that ends in one result chunk (carries tokens, not usage); the provider runs in an ExecutionContext.\n- **Providers**: Claude Code, Codex, Pi exist; the kernel provider is proposed (orange, dashed wires) and would wrap kernel.spawnAgent.\n- **Ford's setup · outside Archon**: kernel.spawnAgent and Token Gateway (100.104.171.122:8793); every provider sends model traffic there.\n- **Event records**: the executor appends workflow_events rows; the proposed kernel provider writes trace_events envelopes; a proposed bridge joins them and must invent or lose containerId, parentEventId and spanId (the \"Archon row lacks\" group).\n\nKey: blue = Archon today, teal = contract types, orange/dashed = proposed, violet = Ford's setup, red = fields the Archon row lacks.",
